  "summary_en": "NITI Aayog's 2018 discussion paper sets out India's national AI strategy (#AIforAll). It prioritises healthcare, agriculture, education, smart cities and smart mobility, and identifies barriers such as skills, data access, privacy and cost. It recommends research centres, skilling, adoption support, a data ecosystem and ethics and privacy frameworks. Embodied AI appears mainly in mobility and agriculture.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Proposes #AIforAll brand: inclusive AI leadership and India as a 'garage' for emerging economies",
   "Targets five focus sectors: healthcare, agriculture, education, smart cities, smart mobility",
   "Recommends core research centres (COREs) and international centres for transformational AI (ICTAIs), with the AIRAWAT shared compute platform",
   "Identifies barriers: expertise, data ecosystems, cost, privacy and security, lack of collaboration",
   "Calls for ethics, privacy and security frameworks, including data anonymisation rules and a data protection law"
  ],
